265
00:11:30,667 --> 00:11:32,367
I'll give you car fare home.

266
00:11:32,400 --> 00:11:34,200
I'm not going home.

267
00:11:34,233 --> 00:11:35,700
Well, where you headed?

268
00:11:35,733 --> 00:11:37,800
That's my business.

269
00:11:37,833 --> 00:11:41,167
You don't seem
to understand, kid.

270
00:11:41,200 --> 00:11:42,567
You're out of business.

271
00:11:42,600 --> 00:11:45,833
You're under bankruptcy
protection from the court.

272
00:11:45,867 --> 00:11:47,233
You had
a hundred bucks here.

273
00:11:47,267 --> 00:11:48,733
How come you're
hopping freights?

274
00:11:48,767 --> 00:11:50,333
Kinda hard to hop a plane.

275
00:11:50,367 --> 00:11:53,567
Well, you aren't used
to traveling this way.

276
00:11:53,600 --> 00:11:55,400
This is something new
to you.

277
00:11:55,433 --> 00:11:57,300
You don't even know how
to handle yourself yet.

278
00:11:57,333 --> 00:11:59,600
I got separated
from my band trip, okay?

279
00:11:59,633 --> 00:11:59,767
Meaning what?

280
00:12:00,967 --> 00:12:03,667
Meaning you don't know
how to hang on to what's yours.

281
00:12:03,700 --> 00:12:05,100
If I give this back to you,

282
00:12:05,133 --> 00:12:06,533
somebody else will just
take it away again.

283
00:12:06,567 --> 00:12:08,867
Good idea. You better hang on
to my clothes then too.

284
00:12:08,900 --> 00:12:10,100
What's your name, kid?

285
00:12:10,133 --> 00:12:11,500
Sex poodle. Oh.

286
00:12:11,533 --> 00:12:13,533
Danny.

287
00:12:13,567 --> 00:12:15,767
Danny winslow.

288
00:12:15,800 --> 00:12:17,700
Bix stoogan.

289
00:12:17,733 --> 00:12:19,233
Big stupid?

290
00:12:19,267 --> 00:12:21,400
Mr. Stupid, can I have
my wallet back now?

291
00:12:26,567 --> 00:12:28,733
War torn Wisconsin.

292
00:12:28,767 --> 00:12:31,733
[Imitates cow]

293
00:12:37,267 --> 00:12:39,467
Wow, you got me a wallet.
And I just lost mine.

294
00:12:39,500 --> 00:12:41,400
If you said you'd stole it,
I'd have kept it.

295
00:12:45,433 --> 00:12:49,633
How's that make you feel?

296
00:12:49,667 --> 00:12:51,133
Well, you better get some sleep,
Danny boy.

297
00:12:51,167 --> 00:12:52,900
I can't sleep now.
I'm too excited.

298
00:12:52,933 --> 00:12:55,233
I think maybe you got
a long way to go.

299
00:12:55,267 --> 00:12:58,667
And I'm gonna
take you there.

300
00:12:58,700 --> 00:13:02,867
Hey, I call the top bunk.

301
00:13:02,900 --> 00:13:05,900
Hey, are we bound for glory
right now, Mr. Big stupid?

302
00:13:08,833 --> 00:13:12,367
Rail. Rail against the dying
of the light.

303
00:13:12,400 --> 00:13:14,033
Rail.

304
00:13:17,033 --> 00:13:18,833
You were incredible.

305
00:13:20,033 --> 00:13:21,033
Bix?

306
00:13:21,067 --> 00:13:22,300
Can I have a glass of water?

307
00:13:22,333 --> 00:13:23,667
Are you asleep?

308
00:13:24,500 --> 00:13:26,333
Yeah.

309
00:13:28,133 --> 00:13:29,133
I'm thinking.

310
00:13:29,167 --> 00:13:30,467
Can we snuggle?

311
00:13:30,500 --> 00:13:32,100
Don't.
You'll weaken the team.

312
00:13:32,133 --> 00:13:34,067
I wrote a poem about you
while you were sleeping.

313
00:13:34,100 --> 00:13:37,467
Where you going, bix?

314
00:13:37,500 --> 00:13:39,700
Back to sleep.

315
00:13:42,433 --> 00:13:43,900
I'm serious.
Wake up and talk to me.

316
00:13:43,933 --> 00:13:44,867
Where you headed?

317
00:13:44,900 --> 00:13:49,067
- This is getting weird.
- Mm-hmm.

318
00:13:49,100 --> 00:13:51,400
Wherever this train's headed.
I ain't particular.

319
00:13:51,433 --> 00:13:53,567
Should we call ahead
and make reservations?

320
00:13:53,600 --> 00:13:57,333
That's what I thought.

321
00:13:57,367 --> 00:13:58,300
I've got an idea.

322
00:13:58,333 --> 00:13:59,933
Toaster pastries.

323
00:13:59,967 --> 00:14:01,533
Congratulations.

324
00:14:01,567 --> 00:14:03,967
Uh, bix, don't laugh
at my footie pajamas

325
00:14:04,000 --> 00:14:07,400
when I put 'em on, okay?

326
00:14:07,433 --> 00:14:09,967
- All right.
- Hop on.

327
00:14:10,000 --> 00:14:11,533
What do you
wanna talk about?

328
00:14:11,567 --> 00:14:14,167
Well, I was thinking about
changing the part in my hair.

329
00:14:14,200 --> 00:14:16,167
Well, I was just thinking.

330
00:14:16,200 --> 00:14:18,233
Since you don't care
where you go,

331
00:14:18,267 --> 00:14:21,367
just so long
as you keep moving,

332
00:14:21,400 --> 00:14:22,933
why can't
we travel together?

333
00:14:22,967 --> 00:14:25,233
I killed a bunch of drifters
and you could be next.

334
00:14:25,267 --> 00:14:28,400
Well, for one thing,
you got 100 bucks, kid.

335
00:14:28,433 --> 00:14:29,900
I don't know whether
you know it or not,

336
00:14:29,933 --> 00:14:31,967
but a traditional vagrant
don't make much money.

337
00:14:32,000 --> 00:14:33,433
They money'll be my part
of the deal.

338
00:14:33,467 --> 00:14:35,600
You'll bring
a sense of style.

339
00:14:35,633 --> 00:14:39,267
I--I'd just like to have
someone to go with.

340
00:14:39,300 --> 00:14:41,300
And I'll give you $10
every time you don't hit me.

341
00:14:41,333 --> 00:14:42,867
It's your loot, man.

342
00:14:42,900 --> 00:14:44,800
I guess we're stuck
with each other.

343
00:14:44,833 --> 00:14:48,467
Dear diary, I think I'm finally
becoming a real vagrant.

344
00:14:48,500 --> 00:14:49,900
Big stupid says
he's gonna teach me

345
00:14:49,933 --> 00:14:52,133
the ins and outs
of drifting.

346
00:14:52,167 --> 00:14:54,267
At my age
I'm gonna be a mother.

347
00:14:54,300 --> 00:14:56,133
Hey, this boxcar's enormous.

348
00:14:56,167 --> 00:14:58,833
Would you move, Danny?

349
00:15:00,033 --> 00:15:02,333
[Horn blaring]

350
00:15:02,367 --> 00:15:04,333
Uh, uh, camera three,
get off the tracks.

351
00:15:04,367 --> 00:15:05,567
Camera three--
oh, dear god!

352
00:15:14,167 --> 00:15:15,100
Ooh.

353
00:15:15,133 --> 00:15:16,600
I woke up and you were there.

354
00:15:16,633 --> 00:15:18,433
I hate that.

355
00:15:18,467 --> 00:15:20,000
What's the matter?

356
00:15:20,033 --> 00:15:21,967
Seven minutes late,
raccoon on the tracks

357
00:15:22,000 --> 00:15:23,667
at Brixton.

358
00:15:23,700 --> 00:15:24,767
Oh, nothing. They're probably
stopping for water.

359
00:15:24,800 --> 00:15:26,433
Is that bad
when they stop for water?

360
00:15:26,467 --> 00:15:28,433
Do you want me to get you
some water, bix?

361
00:15:28,467 --> 00:15:29,533
- There's water--
- shut up, Danny.

362
00:15:29,567 --> 00:15:30,400
Oh.

363
00:15:33,767 --> 00:15:36,233
Hold me.

364
00:15:36,267 --> 00:15:39,667
Oh, it's just as I dreamed
it would be.

365
00:15:39,700 --> 00:15:42,433
Looks like we're about
a mile from town.

366
00:15:42,467 --> 00:15:44,067
Better get off here.

367
00:15:44,100 --> 00:15:45,367
Never mind.

368
00:15:45,400 --> 00:15:47,233
Why don't we just take the train
all the way in?

369
00:15:47,267 --> 00:15:49,400
Sure, all the way in
and right to jail.

370
00:15:49,433 --> 00:15:52,233
Or did you buy a ticket
for this joyride?

371
00:15:52,267 --> 00:15:53,667
She's slowing down.
Come on.

372
00:15:54,667 --> 00:15:57,333
Mr. Big stupid, catch me.

373
00:15:58,367 --> 00:16:00,233
Is this right?
Am I walking with you right?

374
00:16:01,400 --> 00:16:02,667
I'll always remember you,

375
00:16:02,700 --> 00:16:05,367
boxcar number 1837562093.

376
00:16:05,400 --> 00:16:07,233
Goodbye.

377
00:16:07,267 --> 00:16:10,500
I'd really like
to freshen up now.

378
00:16:12,567 --> 00:16:17,233
Gee, I thought Vegas would be
bigger and shinier.

379
00:16:17,267 --> 00:16:21,100
Get off the road,
you drifters.

380
00:16:21,133 --> 00:16:23,867
Like father like bum.

381
00:16:23,900 --> 00:16:26,733
Think about it,
won't you?

382
00:16:26,767 --> 00:16:28,700
Is that a girl,
my lord,

383
00:16:28,733 --> 00:16:30,100
in a flat-bed Ford,

384
00:16:30,133 --> 00:16:31,367
slowing down
to take a look at--

385
00:16:31,400 --> 00:16:33,400
oh, no.

386
00:16:33,433 --> 00:16:36,867
Hey, I want you to take this kid
for me, will ya?

387
00:16:36,900 --> 00:16:40,967
Hey, can we stop
for biscuits and gravy, big?

388
00:16:41,000 --> 00:16:42,900
I think I sat on your keys.

389
00:16:42,933 --> 00:16:44,100
What town are we coming to?

390
00:16:44,133 --> 00:16:45,067
Funky town.

391
00:16:45,100 --> 00:16:46,100
Sherman.

392
00:16:46,133 --> 00:16:47,667
Nice little town.

393
00:16:47,700 --> 00:16:48,633
I'll say.

394
00:16:48,667 --> 00:16:50,400
No ifs ands or buts.

395
00:16:50,433 --> 00:16:53,067
- Two moon junction.
- Whoo-hoo-hoo-hoo!

396
00:16:53,100 --> 00:16:55,100
Laura petrie, no!

397
00:16:55,133 --> 00:16:56,600
Laura petrie, yes!

398
00:16:56,633 --> 00:17:00,800
Actually, guys,
it's Millie helper.

399
00:17:00,833 --> 00:17:03,300
That's real nice, ma'am,
but you're still under arrest.

400
00:17:03,333 --> 00:17:05,933
- See ya later, Carrie.
- You're so very.

401
00:17:05,967 --> 00:17:06,967
[Train horn beeping]

402
00:17:07,000 --> 00:17:08,533
Hey, train'll be in soon.

403
00:17:08,567 --> 00:17:09,800
Oh, it's just another freight.

404
00:17:09,833 --> 00:17:11,267
It'll still be in soon.

405
00:17:11,300 --> 00:17:12,767
Oh, Peggy,
not another one.

406
00:17:12,800 --> 00:17:13,767
Just a half one.

407
00:17:13,800 --> 00:17:14,967
You'll get fat.

408
00:17:15,000 --> 00:17:16,333
Johnny isn't complaining.

409
00:17:16,367 --> 00:17:17,967
Johnny's pretty wild.

410
00:17:18,000 --> 00:17:20,100
You've been seeing a lot
of him lately.

411
00:17:20,133 --> 00:17:21,467
Well, he's better
than nothing.

412
00:17:21,500 --> 00:17:22,500
You haven't tried nothing.

413
00:17:22,533 --> 00:17:23,800
You haven't been
seeing anybody.

414
00:17:23,833 --> 00:17:25,633
You never do.

415
00:17:25,667 --> 00:17:27,633
Oh, I can't talk to boys
the way you do.

416
00:17:27,667 --> 00:17:29,800
That's silly, Carrie.

417
00:17:29,833 --> 00:17:31,667
Besides, who has to talk?

418
00:17:31,700 --> 00:17:33,767
Oh, I get it.

419
00:17:33,800 --> 00:17:35,467
Oh, look who just walked in.

420
00:17:35,500 --> 00:17:37,600
Sherman's answer
to the brainless wonder.

421
00:17:37,633 --> 00:17:38,867
Shh.

422
00:17:38,900 --> 00:17:40,233
Hey, it's Abe Lincoln.

423
00:17:40,267 --> 00:17:43,167
My pa left a list of things
for you to get, Jessie.

424
00:17:43,200 --> 00:17:44,833
Lice shampoo and a comb?

425
00:17:44,867 --> 00:17:47,333
You understand
what you gotta do now?

426
00:17:47,367 --> 00:17:48,867
I don't think you're
getting through, honey.

427
00:17:48,900 --> 00:17:49,967
Try drawing pictures.

428
00:17:50,000 --> 00:17:51,000
Hey, what did I say?

429
00:17:51,033 --> 00:17:53,033
I'm talking to you.

430
00:17:53,933 --> 00:17:55,233
I know.

431
00:17:55,267 --> 00:17:56,567
I just like to look at you.

432
00:17:56,600 --> 00:17:59,967
Oh, wow. Maybe I should leave
you two lovebirds alone.

433
00:18:00,000 --> 00:18:01,133
No.

434
00:18:01,167 --> 00:18:02,633
Supposed to go down
to the store

435
00:18:02,667 --> 00:18:04,367
and get your pa some supplies.
Is that right?

436
00:18:04,400 --> 00:18:06,000
Yes, that's right.

437
00:18:06,033 --> 00:18:07,200
As a young man,

438
00:18:07,233 --> 00:18:08,667
Garrison keillor was shunned
by his friends.

439
00:18:08,700 --> 00:18:10,100
Thank you, Jessie.

440
00:18:10,133 --> 00:18:13,167
[Imitates Frankenstein grunting]

441
00:18:13,200 --> 00:18:17,467
I wish that I
was Jessie's girl.

442
00:18:17,500 --> 00:18:18,400
Ugh.

443
00:18:18,433 --> 00:18:20,400
Smells like
derby canned tamales.

444
00:18:20,433 --> 00:18:21,433
You're trembling.

445
00:18:21,467 --> 00:18:23,233
Am I?

446
00:18:23,267 --> 00:18:24,833
I don't ever want
to be alone with him.

447
00:18:24,867 --> 00:18:26,033
Just the thought of it--

448
00:18:26,067 --> 00:18:28,167
oh, stop it, Terry.
For goodness sakes.

449
00:18:28,200 --> 00:18:29,900
He's as harmless as a pup.

450
00:18:29,933 --> 00:18:30,933
Yeah, cujo.

451
00:18:30,967 --> 00:18:33,333
Everybody knows that.

452
00:18:33,367 --> 00:18:35,567
The poor idiot likes you,
that's all.

453
00:18:35,600 --> 00:18:37,333
The way you're dressed,
who wouldn't leer at you?

454
00:18:37,367 --> 00:18:39,533
What you need
is a man, honey.

455
00:18:39,567 --> 00:18:41,167
I know.

456
00:18:41,200 --> 00:18:42,733
You'll see.
One'll come along.

457
00:18:42,767 --> 00:18:44,500
They always do.

458
00:18:44,533 --> 00:18:47,333
Ha. That's our midge.

459
00:18:47,367 --> 00:18:50,200
* green eyed lady,
sexy lady *

460
00:18:50,233 --> 00:18:51,733
I had enough of you two.

461
00:18:51,767 --> 00:18:56,767
Now get out, out, out!

462
00:18:56,800 --> 00:18:59,233
Big, should I have not put
my head in the driver's lap?

463
00:18:59,267 --> 00:19:01,100
Was that wrong?

464
00:19:02,100 --> 00:19:04,100
Look out, sherman.
Here we come.

465
00:19:04,133 --> 00:19:05,500
Shut up, Danny.

466
00:19:05,533 --> 00:19:08,333
Oh.

467
00:19:08,367 --> 00:19:09,933
Ever been here before?

468
00:19:09,967 --> 00:19:11,767
Small towns
are all the same.

469
00:19:11,800 --> 00:19:13,067
Seen one,
you seen 'em all.

470
00:19:13,100 --> 00:19:14,400
Well,
the zoning's different.

471
00:19:14,433 --> 00:19:16,300
I'm hungry.
Let's get something to eat.

472
00:19:16,333 --> 00:19:17,467
That's a good idea.

473
00:19:17,500 --> 00:19:18,600
You're catching on, kid.

474
00:19:18,633 --> 00:19:22,200
That was very
insightful of you.

475
00:19:22,233 --> 00:19:24,200
We're hungry,
but I thought of it.

476
00:19:24,233 --> 00:19:25,867
You know, do you think
that could be my new job, Vic?

477
00:19:25,900 --> 00:19:26,900
Deciding when to eat?

478
00:19:26,933 --> 00:19:28,433
- Shut up, Danny.
- Oh.

479
00:19:28,467 --> 00:19:29,500
You won't tell your old man
I was late, will you?

480
00:19:29,533 --> 00:19:30,467
No, of course not, but...

481
00:19:30,500 --> 00:19:31,867
But what?

482
00:19:31,900 --> 00:19:32,800
Shouldn't have brought her
in here with you.

483
00:19:32,833 --> 00:19:33,767
Ah, what's the harm?

484
00:19:33,800 --> 00:19:35,933
You know how pa
feels about her.

485
00:19:35,967 --> 00:19:36,900
He's told you time and again

486
00:19:36,933 --> 00:19:38,400
not to let Sadie in here.

487
00:19:38,433 --> 00:19:40,633
How's he gonna know
unless you tell him?

488
00:19:40,667 --> 00:19:41,600
Let me worry about it.

489
00:19:41,633 --> 00:19:43,267
Hey, Mel, kiss my grits.

490
00:19:43,300 --> 00:19:45,767
Tom,
don't ever say that again.

491
00:19:45,800 --> 00:19:46,967
Okay, what'll it be?

492
00:19:47,000 --> 00:19:48,433
Well, first,
a little respect.

493
00:19:48,467 --> 00:19:49,967
We ain't bummin' a meal.

494
00:19:50,000 --> 00:19:51,900
Oh, a money man, huh?

495
00:19:51,933 --> 00:19:54,000
Well,
now ain't that interesting.

496
00:19:54,033 --> 00:19:56,233
You're gonna have to excuse
the looks of this place.

497
00:19:56,267 --> 00:19:58,767
We ain't used to catering
to the carriage trade.

498
00:19:58,800 --> 00:20:01,167
Well, do you think you could
get back here with a menu

499
00:20:01,200 --> 00:20:02,833
before the food goes bad?

500
00:20:02,867 --> 00:20:05,667
Food's bad already.

501
00:20:05,700 --> 00:20:07,300
What is this, the sad cafe?

502
00:20:07,333 --> 00:20:09,033
Go on up there
and wait on those clowns.

503
00:20:09,067 --> 00:20:11,633
[All imitate circus music]

504
00:20:11,667 --> 00:20:13,433
Hi, I'm midge.

505
00:20:13,467 --> 00:20:15,000
Can I start you out
with some grilled mahi mahi

506
00:20:15,033 --> 00:20:16,267
and a grapefruit cream sauce?

507
00:20:16,300 --> 00:20:18,133
Don't fall in love
with US, baby.

508
00:20:18,167 --> 00:20:21,933
We'll hurt you every time.

509
00:20:21,967 --> 00:20:23,767
Have you made up
your minds yet?

510
00:20:23,800 --> 00:20:25,133
Have I ever.

511
00:20:25,167 --> 00:20:25,933
- Aoogah! Aoogah!
- Ding! Ding! Ding!

512
00:20:25,967 --> 00:20:26,900
- Dive! Dive!

513
00:20:26,933 --> 00:20:28,400
Oh, you mean the order.

514
00:20:28,433 --> 00:20:31,133
Well, I'll have, uh,
scrambled eggs and coffee.

515
00:20:31,167 --> 00:20:33,000
Okay, you want juice, salad,

516
00:20:33,033 --> 00:20:35,667
roll, grapefruit half,
or pudding?

517
00:20:35,700 --> 00:20:38,500
Rosie, the early years.

518
00:20:38,533 --> 00:20:40,000
I didn't think life
could get any worse.

519
00:20:40,033 --> 00:20:42,567
I'm gonna go turn
on the gas.

520
00:20:43,633 --> 00:20:44,967
I've got a feeling

521
00:20:45,000 --> 00:20:46,900
you're spending the rest
of our money right here.

522
00:20:46,933 --> 00:20:48,233
You're not ready
for quips yet, Danny.

523
00:20:48,267 --> 00:20:49,467
Well, now, what I got in mind,
Danny boy,

524
00:20:49,500 --> 00:20:52,367
shouldn't cost me.

