785
00:30:52,600 --> 00:30:53,533
Like you?

786
00:30:53,567 --> 00:30:54,567
Just reading Cathy.

787
00:30:54,600 --> 00:30:55,633
Leave me out of it.

788
00:30:55,667 --> 00:30:57,467
- Oh, bix...
- Will you change me?

789
00:30:57,500 --> 00:30:59,700
Why do we have to fight
if we don't want to?

790
00:30:59,733 --> 00:31:00,733
Testosterone.

791
00:31:00,767 --> 00:31:02,033
- Why can't we just...
- Love.

792
00:31:02,067 --> 00:31:03,533
Because that's the way
things are, kid.

793
00:31:03,567 --> 00:31:05,067
Uh-huh. Uh-huh.

794
00:31:05,100 --> 00:31:06,133
I told you once
it ain't easy

795
00:31:06,167 --> 00:31:07,933
to hold on to what's yours.

796
00:31:07,967 --> 00:31:10,900
Sometimes you gotta
fight for it.

797
00:31:10,933 --> 00:31:14,433
Well, we better not
keep them waiting.

798
00:31:14,467 --> 00:31:16,433
Yeah, they might get angry
and hit US.

799
00:31:16,467 --> 00:31:19,433
I guess.

800
00:31:19,467 --> 00:31:20,867
Well, let's get down
to business.

801
00:31:20,900 --> 00:31:22,467
Okay.

802
00:31:22,500 --> 00:31:23,633
There's four of them.

803
00:31:23,667 --> 00:31:26,267
And one of you.

804
00:31:26,300 --> 00:31:28,033
- Come here.
- Okay.

805
00:31:28,067 --> 00:31:29,200
Now what I'm gonna do, see,

806
00:31:29,233 --> 00:31:30,600
is I'm gonna kill you

807
00:31:30,633 --> 00:31:32,500
and strap you around my body
for armor.

808
00:31:32,533 --> 00:31:35,500
...two of US.

809
00:31:35,533 --> 00:31:36,533
That just
don't come out right.

810
00:31:36,567 --> 00:31:38,000
Well, what's so funny?

811
00:31:38,033 --> 00:31:41,833
Well, any way you look at it,
we're gonna get killed.

812
00:31:41,867 --> 00:31:43,700
I don't wanna be a hobo.

813
00:31:43,733 --> 00:31:45,533
I wanna be a nurse.

814
00:31:47,767 --> 00:31:50,033
Uh, I forgot my comb.

815
00:31:50,067 --> 00:31:51,400
Comb over here.

816
00:31:51,433 --> 00:31:54,033
Uh, which one of you
speaks stupid?

817
00:31:54,067 --> 00:31:55,833
Jerry just said to tell you
here'll make a deal.

818
00:31:55,867 --> 00:31:57,400
I'll give you five dollars

819
00:31:57,433 --> 00:31:59,200
if you got a hardboiled egg
in your purse.

820
00:31:59,233 --> 00:32:01,100
Hand over the wallet
nice and peaceful

821
00:32:01,133 --> 00:32:02,400
and you can walk out of here

822
00:32:02,433 --> 00:32:04,400
the same way you came in.

823
00:32:04,433 --> 00:32:06,867
Well, that don't make sense.

824
00:32:06,900 --> 00:32:08,167
I thought
it didn't sound right.

825
00:32:08,200 --> 00:32:09,167
We give you our wallet,

826
00:32:09,200 --> 00:32:11,000
we go out of here
flat broke.

827
00:32:11,033 --> 00:32:14,000
And, man, that ain't
the way we came in.

828
00:32:14,033 --> 00:32:15,733
That's your answer then?

829
00:32:15,767 --> 00:32:17,033
That's it, Sonny.

830
00:32:17,067 --> 00:32:18,200
Okay. All right.

831
00:32:18,233 --> 00:32:20,100
Well, I'll just--

832
00:32:20,133 --> 00:32:22,867
I'm gonna let Jerry know,
and I'll get back to you.

833
00:32:22,900 --> 00:32:25,400
Okay.

834
00:32:25,433 --> 00:32:27,300
I think he likes me.

835
00:32:29,467 --> 00:32:31,200
Can I have change for a 50.

836
00:32:31,233 --> 00:32:33,433
What a dummy.

837
00:32:35,467 --> 00:32:36,467
Come on.

838
00:32:36,500 --> 00:32:37,533
[Whistles]
Here, boy.

839
00:32:37,567 --> 00:32:39,367
Come on, Danny.
There he goes.

840
00:32:39,400 --> 00:32:44,300
Uh, sir, can you change this
back into a 50?

841
00:32:44,333 --> 00:32:47,467
Well, I didn't expect to spend
the whole 50 bucks in there.

842
00:32:47,500 --> 00:32:50,633
We're flat broke now!

843
00:32:50,667 --> 00:32:52,667
They got away.
That was brilliant.

844
00:32:55,933 --> 00:32:58,333
Certainly not worth mugging US

845
00:32:58,367 --> 00:33:00,400
for, um, 75 cents.

846
00:33:00,433 --> 00:33:02,933
The dark side of mayberry.

847
00:33:02,967 --> 00:33:04,467
Yeah, if Andy were here,

848
00:33:04,500 --> 00:33:06,900
he'd outwit them
with some homespun wisdom.

849
00:33:06,933 --> 00:33:08,967
I feel sorry
for the unfortunate mugger

850
00:33:09,000 --> 00:33:11,433
who mugged US.

851
00:33:11,467 --> 00:33:16,900
Hey, um, what's the downside
of running again, big?

852
00:33:16,933 --> 00:33:18,800
[Imitating ed Sullivan]
Really good show tonight...

853
00:33:18,833 --> 00:33:20,433
Really good show.

854
00:33:20,467 --> 00:33:21,933
- See this alley?
- It's where you're gonna die.

855
00:33:21,967 --> 00:33:23,200
Pay attention.

856
00:33:23,233 --> 00:33:24,933
- Ow.
- See this alley?

857
00:33:24,967 --> 00:33:26,433
Yeah.

858
00:33:26,467 --> 00:33:27,667
This is where it'll be then.

859
00:33:27,700 --> 00:33:28,767
Now you do like I say...

860
00:33:28,800 --> 00:33:29,800
Ow!

861
00:33:29,833 --> 00:33:31,433
Remember, folks,
a backhand

862
00:33:31,467 --> 00:33:33,533
will knock him cold
for hours.

863
00:33:35,133 --> 00:33:36,100
Hey, it's got
all the furnishings

864
00:33:36,133 --> 00:33:38,333
from their boxcar.

865
00:33:38,367 --> 00:33:41,467
What--
what happened?

866
00:33:50,267 --> 00:33:52,333
I'll get a tricorder
reading, captain.

867
00:33:54,400 --> 00:33:58,500
[Imitating cat]

868
00:33:58,533 --> 00:34:01,500
Frankie valliand the four
seasons of the apocalypse.

869
00:34:01,533 --> 00:34:03,333
[Chuckles]

870
00:34:03,367 --> 00:34:08,200
I'll give 'em a manicure
they'll never forget.

871
00:34:08,233 --> 00:34:10,567
[Humming]

872
00:34:14,600 --> 00:34:17,833
Oh, this is the alley
where fonzie was introduced.

873
00:34:17,867 --> 00:34:19,067
Ooh.

874
00:34:19,100 --> 00:34:24,167
Hey, sit on it.

875
00:34:24,200 --> 00:34:25,400
Plop, plop, fist, fist,

876
00:34:25,433 --> 00:34:27,100
oh, what a fight it is.

877
00:34:27,133 --> 00:34:29,033
- Where's the other one?
- I don't know. I can't see him.

878
00:34:29,067 --> 00:34:30,400
What are you waiting for,
Danny?

879
00:34:30,433 --> 00:34:33,867
Don't hurt me.
I have this glass jaw thingy.

880
00:34:33,900 --> 00:34:36,600
Danny likes you, mister.

881
00:34:36,633 --> 00:34:38,400
Oh, look out.
I dropped my--

882
00:34:38,433 --> 00:34:39,567
okay, I got it.
Okay.

883
00:34:41,433 --> 00:34:43,467
Spartacus.

884
00:34:47,300 --> 00:34:49,433
Frodo is in
one of those barrels.

885
00:34:49,467 --> 00:34:51,900
Oh, that smacks
of tolkienism.

886
00:34:51,933 --> 00:34:55,067
Aah!

887
00:34:55,100 --> 00:34:57,200
Watch out for the recycling.

888
00:34:57,233 --> 00:34:59,733
Oh.

889
00:34:59,767 --> 00:35:03,133
He's trying
to uncomfortable him to death.

890
00:35:03,167 --> 00:35:05,100
Oh, he looks good in a choker.

891
00:35:06,400 --> 00:35:09,500
[Imitates muffled speech]

892
00:35:13,133 --> 00:35:18,500
Must...save...spock.

893
00:35:18,533 --> 00:35:24,767
What's that little guy
doin' in there?

894
00:35:24,800 --> 00:35:26,467
Crosby, stills,
Nash, and young

895
00:35:26,500 --> 00:35:29,700
have creative differences.

896
00:35:29,733 --> 00:35:32,400
Long may you punch.

897
00:35:36,400 --> 00:35:40,800
It's Donny most and Joel grey
in a fight to the death.

898
00:35:40,833 --> 00:35:44,333
You guys need anything
in there?

899
00:35:44,367 --> 00:35:46,433
The cross
and the switchblade.

900
00:35:50,533 --> 00:35:51,767
Mom!

901
00:35:51,800 --> 00:35:54,000
What were you doing
down there, kid?

902
00:35:54,033 --> 00:35:55,133
Come on, kid.

903
00:35:55,167 --> 00:35:57,333
Let's get back
and get you fixed up.

904
00:35:57,367 --> 00:35:59,133
What about your date?

905
00:35:59,167 --> 00:36:00,467
Forget it.
Ain't that important.

906
00:36:00,500 --> 00:36:02,133
Huh?

907
00:36:04,600 --> 00:36:07,067
Now, wait a sec.
I'm just gonna pop this.

908
00:36:07,100 --> 00:36:09,200
Man, have you got
a lot to learn.

909
00:36:09,233 --> 00:36:11,033
Hold still.

910
00:36:11,067 --> 00:36:14,200
Now, the idea is to keep
your face away from his fist,

911
00:36:14,233 --> 00:36:16,467
not put it out there
where he can find it.

912
00:36:16,500 --> 00:36:17,767
Guess I'm not much
of a fighter.

913
00:36:17,800 --> 00:36:18,867
What are you
whispering for?

914
00:36:18,900 --> 00:36:20,000
It ain't no secret.

915
00:36:20,033 --> 00:36:22,500
How about that guy
I groined in the knee?

916
00:36:22,533 --> 00:36:24,333
You know,
first thing in the morning

917
00:36:24,367 --> 00:36:25,833
we're gonna have
to get some new clothes.

918
00:36:25,867 --> 00:36:27,333
Sheriff sees US in these rags,

919
00:36:27,367 --> 00:36:28,600
he'll throw US in jail
for vagrancy.

920
00:36:28,633 --> 00:36:29,967
Is that constitutional?

921
00:36:30,000 --> 00:36:32,000
- Bix.
- Yeah.

922
00:36:32,033 --> 00:36:34,333
Anymore of those...

923
00:36:34,367 --> 00:36:36,833
I was scared.

924
00:36:36,867 --> 00:36:38,600
If you hadn't have been there,
I would have run.

925
00:36:38,633 --> 00:36:39,767
I almost did anyway.

926
00:36:39,800 --> 00:36:42,700
What a wuss.

927
00:36:42,733 --> 00:36:44,967
Well, we're all scared
sometimes, kid.

928
00:36:45,000 --> 00:36:47,400
When you're in a spot like
tonight, you have two choices--

929
00:36:47,433 --> 00:36:49,867
you can stay and face it
and be afraid,

930
00:36:49,900 --> 00:36:52,633
or you can run
and be ashamed.

931
00:36:52,667 --> 00:36:55,033
It's up to you which
is easiest to live with.

932
00:36:55,067 --> 00:36:58,067
I'll take the latter.

933
00:36:58,100 --> 00:36:59,400
That ain't too bad.

934
00:36:59,433 --> 00:37:01,467
Plastic surgeon
fix you up in no time.

935
00:37:01,500 --> 00:37:03,867
Take a look.

936
00:37:03,900 --> 00:37:06,167
So am I supposed to look
like a Picasso painting?

937
00:37:06,200 --> 00:37:07,900
My dad would never
believe this.

938
00:37:07,933 --> 00:37:10,267
You two didn't get along
too good, huh?

939
00:37:10,300 --> 00:37:11,767
Well, sure.
He's quite a guy.

940
00:37:11,800 --> 00:37:13,033
A lawyer.

941
00:37:13,067 --> 00:37:15,067
Well, level with me, kid.

942
00:37:15,100 --> 00:37:17,400
What's this
back alley trip for?

943
00:37:17,433 --> 00:37:18,867
Well, you may as well know.

944
00:37:18,900 --> 00:37:22,600
I'm the prince
from lichtenstein, big.

945
00:37:22,633 --> 00:37:24,367
Said they were getting
a divorce.

946
00:37:24,400 --> 00:37:26,633
Dad made it clear
it was my fault.

947
00:37:26,667 --> 00:37:30,833
Just like that, he said.

948
00:37:30,867 --> 00:37:33,933
So 19 years have been
a waste of time.

949
00:37:33,967 --> 00:37:36,400
Oh, you can see the string.
Look.

950
00:37:36,433 --> 00:37:39,433
Well, so you cut out.
You ran away.

951
00:37:39,467 --> 00:37:41,833
How do you choose
between two people

952
00:37:41,867 --> 00:37:43,700
who have always
seemed like one to you.

953
00:37:43,733 --> 00:37:44,967
Ew.

954
00:37:45,000 --> 00:37:46,033
I've never had that problem.

955
00:37:46,067 --> 00:37:47,567
I wouldn't know
what to tell you.

956
00:37:47,600 --> 00:37:48,767
You're on your own
on this one, Danny.

957
00:37:48,800 --> 00:37:51,933
Crowding me into a corner.

958
00:37:51,967 --> 00:37:54,033
Danny,
this isn't the answer.

959
00:37:54,067 --> 00:37:55,600
My dad's man to man talks,

960
00:37:55,633 --> 00:37:56,567
I couldn't think straight.

961
00:37:56,600 --> 00:37:57,800
I had to get away from them.

962
00:37:57,833 --> 00:37:59,700
This is not your
induction physical, Danny.

963
00:37:59,733 --> 00:38:00,800
Maybe without them pushing

964
00:38:00,833 --> 00:38:02,400
I can work things out
for myself.

965
00:38:05,200 --> 00:38:07,533
Ah, I'm gonna
take some money

966
00:38:07,567 --> 00:38:10,267
out of the till for booze,
okay, honey?

967
00:38:12,833 --> 00:38:14,800
We made over $5 today.

968
00:38:14,833 --> 00:38:16,800
That's a lot for these days.

969
00:38:20,233 --> 00:38:25,200
Ah, 9:00,
business goes under.

970
00:38:25,233 --> 00:38:26,233
Aah!

971
00:38:26,267 --> 00:38:27,233
Your dad's a lawyer.

972
00:38:27,267 --> 00:38:29,000
Does he make good money?

973
00:38:29,033 --> 00:38:31,300
He's always been able
to give me

974
00:38:31,333 --> 00:38:33,100
whatever I wanted.
Within reason.

975
00:38:33,133 --> 00:38:34,900
Tell me another story, big.

976
00:38:34,933 --> 00:38:36,633
I guess you'd say
we're as close

977
00:38:36,667 --> 00:38:39,333
as a guy and his dad
can be.

978
00:38:39,367 --> 00:38:40,967
Big, was it something
I said in the fight?

979
00:38:41,000 --> 00:38:41,933
What's funny now?

980
00:38:41,967 --> 00:38:44,800
Sounds like my old man.

981
00:38:44,833 --> 00:38:47,100
We were real close too.

982
00:38:47,133 --> 00:38:49,667
Took me
everywhere he went.

983
00:38:49,700 --> 00:38:51,733
I knew every beer joint
in town

984
00:38:51,767 --> 00:38:53,000
by the time I was eight.

985
00:38:53,033 --> 00:38:55,067
That's somebody's
ideal childhood.

986
00:38:55,100 --> 00:38:58,400
He gave me a lot
of things too.

987
00:38:58,433 --> 00:39:00,633
Mostly his fist in my face.

988
00:39:00,667 --> 00:39:04,967
Did he swing it, or just
place it there gently?

989
00:39:05,000 --> 00:39:09,200
Well, I'm gonna go
continue the cycle.

990
00:39:09,233 --> 00:39:11,733
Oh, I know
these kinda guys, honey.

991
00:39:11,767 --> 00:39:12,767
He's a drifter.

992
00:39:12,800 --> 00:39:15,467
They never stay put
very long.

993
00:39:15,500 --> 00:39:19,933
He might have left town
last night.

994
00:39:19,967 --> 00:39:22,967
Here's the lunch rush.

995
00:39:23,000 --> 00:39:24,200
Shall I?

996
00:39:24,233 --> 00:39:25,167
No, pa.
I'll take their order.

997
00:39:25,200 --> 00:39:26,967
Back off, dad.
He's mine.

998
00:39:27,000 --> 00:39:27,800
- Hi, Carrie.
- Hi.

999
00:39:27,833 --> 00:39:29,500
- Hi.
- Hi!

1000
00:39:29,533 --> 00:39:31,167
- Hi.
- How ya doing?

1001
00:39:31,200 --> 00:39:32,400
What are you
going to have?

1002
00:39:32,433 --> 00:39:33,867
Oh, I don't know.
What do you got?

1003
00:39:33,900 --> 00:39:34,967
Anger and resentment.

1004
00:39:35,000 --> 00:39:37,000
I waited for you
last night.

1005
00:39:37,033 --> 00:39:38,333
- Oh, yeah.
- Yeah.

1006
00:39:38,367 --> 00:39:39,667
Well... [coughs]

1007
00:39:39,700 --> 00:39:41,700
Well, something came up
out of nowhere, and...

1008
00:39:41,733 --> 00:39:43,133
I had a trans-species
experience last night.

1009
00:39:43,167 --> 00:39:45,967
Landed all over his face.

1010
00:39:46,000 --> 00:39:47,633
Oh.

1011
00:39:47,667 --> 00:39:49,467
Ain't no kiddin', Carrie.
I'm sorry.

1012
00:39:49,500 --> 00:39:51,567
Let's make it for tonight.
What do you say?

1013
00:39:51,600 --> 00:39:52,833
Same time?

1014
00:39:52,867 --> 00:39:55,533
All right. Tonight.

1015
00:39:55,567 --> 00:40:00,467
Sucker.

1016
00:40:00,500 --> 00:40:01,433
Hi!

1017
00:40:01,467 --> 00:40:02,433
- Hi.
- Hi.

1018
00:40:02,467 --> 00:40:03,533
- Can you imagine?
- What?

1019
00:40:03,567 --> 00:40:05,300
Two hours I waited
for him last night.

1020
00:40:05,333 --> 00:40:06,233
Who?
What are you talking about?

1021
00:40:06,267 --> 00:40:07,700
Johnny. Who else?

1022
00:40:07,733 --> 00:40:09,600
Two hours I wait,
and he doesn't even show up.

1023
00:40:09,633 --> 00:40:10,567
Honestly, Carrie,
sometimes I don't even...

1024
00:40:10,600 --> 00:40:16,567
Ixnay, Ellie may.

1025
00:40:16,600 --> 00:40:19,833
I did it again, big.

1026
00:40:19,867 --> 00:40:21,600
Hello there.

1027
00:40:21,633 --> 00:40:23,267
Uh, hi.
Right back at ya.

1028
00:40:23,300 --> 00:40:24,267
This is big.

1029
00:40:24,300 --> 00:40:25,833
And this is, uh...

1030
00:40:25,867 --> 00:40:27,500
This is Danny.

1031
00:40:27,533 --> 00:40:29,567
Hi.

1032
00:40:29,600 --> 00:40:31,700
You're kinda cute
for a boy, hmm?

1033
00:40:31,733 --> 00:40:33,867
What happened to your face?

1034
00:40:33,900 --> 00:40:35,867
What happened to my face,
big stupid?

1035
00:40:35,900 --> 00:40:38,700
...shaving.

1036
00:40:38,733 --> 00:40:40,933
And the moment collapses.

1037
00:40:40,967 --> 00:40:43,233
Got a dime?

1038
00:40:43,267 --> 00:40:44,233
- [Scoffs]
- Sure.

1039
00:40:44,267 --> 00:40:46,033
I got 5,000 dimes.

1040
00:40:46,067 --> 00:40:47,467
Follow me.

1041
00:40:49,333 --> 00:40:51,567
Ah, do you like aqualung?

1042
00:40:54,233 --> 00:40:58,500
[Jazz music starts]

1043
00:40:58,533 --> 00:41:00,533
* leather coat *

